  "title": "G major needs one sharp",
  "summary": "Build a major scale on G with the formula, and one black key appears.",
  "minutes": 5,
  "steps": [
    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Building G major",
      "body": "Start on G and follow the formula W W H W W W H: G, A, B, C, D, E. A whole step up from E lands on F♯, not F. Then a half step brings you to G. So G major is **G A B C D E F♯ G**.\n\n**Why it matters:** this is why songs in G use F♯. It belongs to the scale, so your hand plays that one black key.",
