    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "One letter each",
      "body": "A scale uses each letter once. G major already has an F (as F♯), so it has no plain F, and no G♭ either.\n\n**Why it matters:** this rule is why each scale has one correct spelling, and you will lean on it to name sharps and flats correctly.",
